:R-HSA-933543  a            owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Fas-AssociatedDeathDomain (FADD) and receptor interacting protein 1 (RIP1) are death domain containing molecules that interact with the C-terminal portion of IPS-1 and induce NF-kB through interaction and activation of initiator caspases (caspase-8 and -10). Caspases are usually involved in apoptosis and inflammation but they also exhibit nonapoptotic functions. These nonapoptotic caspase functions involve prodomain-mediated activation of NF-kB. Processed caspases (caspase-8/10) encoding the DED (death effector domain) strongly activate NF-kB. The exact mechanism by which caspases mediate NF-kB activation is unclear, but the prodomains of caspase-8/10 may act as a scaffolding and allow the recruitment of the IKK complex in association with other signaling molecules." ;
        rdfs:label          "NF-kB activation through FADD/RIP-1 pathway mediated by caspase-8 and -10" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Garapati, P V, 2010-08-02" , "Edited: Garapati, P V, 2010-08-02" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Reviewed: Kawai, T, Akira, S, 2010-10-30" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-933543" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-168928/R-HSA-168928> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

